  {
   "id": "BUFvurxuTXkJ",
   "from": "Jonathan Rosenblatt",
   "author": "a305e65fa9dfb74d",
   "date": "2014-08-27T10:42:15Z",
   "subject": "Re: [Israel RUG] סכומי ביניים",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">(a) Readability could be improved. Recall that future-self will have to understand the code. I would loop over categories of y as you will lose nothing in efficiency (by() simply wraps around tapply() which is nothing but a loop), but will gain on readability. <div>\r\n\r\n<br></div><div>(b) I think that rowSums and colSums are slightly more efficiency that apply(X,2,sum).</div><div><br></div><div>(c) The dplyr package is super efficient for data manipulations. You might get good performance by compounding dplyr::group_by and dplyr::summarise. It is actually a package worth knowing anyhow....</div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div><br></div>\r\n<div><br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
